WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.325
Why does a boat stay upright?

2
00:00:02.575 --> 00:00:04.850
And why, some days, doesn’t she?

3
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:09.400
Today’s lesson answers both, and it comes down to three letters.

4
00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:11.475
Look at the diagram.

5
00:00:11.725 --> 00:00:14.275
G is the center of gravity.

6
00:00:14.525 --> 00:00:17.450
It’s where all the weight acts, and it pulls down.

7
00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:23.975
B is the center of buoyancy, the center of the underwater part of the hull, and it pushes up.

8
00:00:24.225 --> 00:00:26.000
Now heel the boat.

9
00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.050
What happens to B?

10
00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:33.850
It moves toward the low side, because more of the hull is underwater there.

11
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:42.000
So now gravity pulls down in one place, and buoyancy pushes up in another, and together they twist the boat back upright.

12
00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:44.150
That’s the righting arm.

13
00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:51.175
The third letter is M, the metacenter: the point where the line straight up from B crosses the centerline.

14
00:00:51.425 --> 00:00:55.800
And the distance from G up to M is the metacentric height, G M.

15
00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:59.675
The bigger the G M, the more firmly she stands up.
